node -e '
const fs=require("fs");
let p="plan.md", s=fs.readFileSync(p,"utf8");
const a="- [ ] 2 roofs: 18 shed bands, palette RoofTile, pediment, compluvium void (E06 E18 E02 E27)";
if(!s.includes(a)) throw new Error("checklist line not found");
s=s.replace(a,"- [x] 2 roofs: 18 shed bands, palette RoofTile, compluvium void (E06 E18 E27); pediment (E02) NOT placed: refused by the shell\x27s air, see NOTES FROM THE ROOFS PART");
s=s.replace(/
*$/,"

## NOTES FROM THE ROOFS PART

- The 18 ROOFS bands are built (parts/roofs.mjs), each on a scratch grid and written back inside the plan box. Reason: roof() reads walls with raw coordinates but writes through set(), so on SiteGrid it reads the walls 4 cells off, and its eaves at x=-1 or y=10 grow the grid and shift every later part.
- Overhang is 0 on every band: an overhang of 1 would put eave cells on x=-1, x=36, z=-1 and inside the compluvium void (x15, z11/18).
- Pediment NOT placed: runParts refuses any write into a cell an earlier part wrote, air included, and the shell carved (16..19, 6..7, 0) to air, so the 6 pediment cells are refused. Needs the shell to leave those cells unowned (or the pediment to move into the shell).
- Pitch 0.5 is the tool\x27s lowest step. Bands 9 deep (RA, RE, RG) rise to y10; the scratch writeback drops the course above y9, so their ridge sits at y9 (flat cap). Plan wants ridges at y9 (pitch ~1/3), which the ladder cannot give without a pitch bypass.
- make.sh roof step (whole-building --dry-run) auto-detects the building as one roof: it warns ROOF_TOO_TALL and ROOF_BIG_PLANE on the building as a whole. Per band there is no height warning beyond the y10 ridges above.
");
fs.writeFileSync(p,s);
p="elements.md"; s=fs.readFileSync(p,"utf8");
s=s.replace(/
*$/,"

Built by the roofs part (ticked): E06, E18, E27. E02 pediment NOT placed (refused by the shell\x27s owned air at (16..19, 6..7, 0); see plan.md NOTES FROM THE ROOFS PART).
");
fs.writeFileSync(p,s);' && tail -3 elements.md && grep -n "2 roofs" plan.md && date

